WEBVTT

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.220
<i>I'm in Ikaho Hot Springs, in Gunma.</i>

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.100
<i>Honoka-chan invited me to hang out here.</i>

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.250
That's Ikaho Shrine.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.980
It's the end of the stone steps.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.930
All right, let's go straight to the top!

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:50.610
Yeah.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.740
<i>I wonder if Hinata and Kokona-chan 
are well on their way up.</i>

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.610
Hinata-san?

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.010
I'm okay.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.400
<b>Everyone's Own Views</b>

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.400
<b>Akasaka Boys' Nature House</b>

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.510
I'm so tired!

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.860
Let's take a break.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.170
It's tougher than I thought.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.380
I thought this mountain would be easier.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.620
I suppose that's the peak over there.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.480
It looks pretty close.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.170
Yeah, we're almost there now.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.600
All right, let's recharge for 
the last leg of the trip.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.420
<b>Ogura Youkan</b>

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.420
Youkan!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.890
It's energy food.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:40.440
Yup.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.090
Thank you!

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.870
So sweet!

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.230
It's revitalizing.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:48.980
Yeah!

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.970
<i>I wonder if Aoi's having fun 
with Honoka-chan about now.</i>

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.730
364...

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.310
365!

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.460
We made it to the top!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.860
Well done.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.120
<i>I wonder if it's because of all the mountain 
climbing that I'm not too exhausted.</i>

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.310
<i>I should be stronger than I used to be.</i>

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.280
It's like the river's turned 
red with the leaves.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.930
The hot spring has a lot of iron in it.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.650
It turns this color when 
it's exposed to the air.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.970
That's why they call it the golden bath.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.290
I see.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.800
You can drink at that fountain over there.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.530
Drink what? The hot spring water?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.520
Yeah. It's supposed to be good for you.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.030
<b>Ikaho Hot Spring Drinking Spot</b>

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:44.050
Hot Spring Water

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.750
Okay, for health.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.480
Oh, but...

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.060
It smells metallic!

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.810
It doesn't taste that good.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.540
You could have told me.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.820
I still think you should bathe in 
hot spring water rather than drink it.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.540
No kidding.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.550
<b>Open-air bath
Ikaho Hot Springs</b>

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.930
Bathing is better.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.080
Wait, you're actually going to?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.390
We really should, since we're here.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.550
But, um...

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.930
Er, I mean...

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.780
Oh, towels!

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.010
I didn't bring a towel.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:12.940
It's okay.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.420
I brought one for you, too.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.940
Oh.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.860
<i>Th-The changing room is outside!</i>

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.250
<i>I-I'm supposed to change here?</i>

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.800
Use this.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.330
Gunma-chan!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.560
It's so cute!

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.780
It's the original towel they sell here. 
It comes in different colors.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.400
<i>I think I'll buy one for Kokona-chan.</i>

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.570
Where do they sell these?

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.340
At the entrance.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.430
What's wrong?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.340
Nothing.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.010
<i>Oh, whatever!</i>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.350
<b>Please shower before entering.</b>

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.480
It feels so good.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.200
This is the closest bath to the 
spring, so it's really good.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.980
Oh, really?

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.390
I think I'm glad I went for it.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.070
I wish Hinata-chan and Kokona-chan 
could've made it, too.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.840
Yeah.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.870
Maybe I should have dragged them here.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:14.200
Hinata-chan must have had her own plans, too.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.070
We'll come back again sometime.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.380
With the others next time.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:19.500
Right?

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:21.540
Yeah.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.120
We made it!

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.020
<b>Japan's Top 100 Mountains
Mt. Akagi</b>

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.020
<b>Jizoudake</b>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.750
We're at the peak!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.280
We did it!

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.610
Darn, it's too cloudy to see far off.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.600
Too bad. We walked all the way up here, too.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.260
The fall colors here are pretty, though.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.120
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.720
Let's make this beautiful 
scenery our tea snack, then.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.630
T-Tea snack?

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.250
It looks so good!

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.120
You made all this?

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.020
Yes, I baked them last night.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.040
Wow!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.450
I've always wanted to try having 
tea time at a mountain peak.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.520
It's pretty amazing that you 
can do this, Kokona-chan.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.770
I'm really bad at fancy stuff like this.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:25.100
The people who flatter me like that 
are the reason I like doing it.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.280
I'm not just flattering you.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.030
Here you go.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.500
Have it while it's hot.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:31.740
Thanks.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.720
These cookies are good!

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.730
I'm glad.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.460
I have scones, too.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.040
Thank you!

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.010
Hinata-san!

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.960
They're angels' bridges.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.670
I guess cloudy weather isn't always so bad.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.620
I'm glad we came here.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.300
Yeah.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.580
<i>If only Aoi were here...</i>

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.310
I'm planning on taking us 
to Haruna Shrine next.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.470
<b>Ikaho Glass
Wooden Toys</b>

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.470
It has a famous spiritual power spot.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:38.030
Since Onii— my brother's here, 
we can get a ride.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.250
Honoka!

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.480
You're back.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.420
The water's nice.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.520
Ikaho Hot Springs never disappoint.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.180
Right, Honoka?

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.190
Honoka?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.230
What's wrong, Honoka?

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.700
At least answer me!

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.100
I thought you couldn't hear me.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.910
What's wrong?

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.380
You're usually like, "Onii-chan, 
I'm getting in with you."

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.200
I don't say that!

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.640
Be quiet and drive!

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.380
Aw, come on!

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.960
No wonder it's a power spot.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.730
It feels like there's some 
kind of mysterious power here.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:27.020
You should make a wish if 
there's anything you want.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.010
It's supposed to grant any wish.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.110
Really?

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:33.110
All right, then...

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:36.110
<b>I wish to make it up Mt. Fuji</b>

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:37.120
Mt. Fuji?

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:37.890
Yeah.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.470
I'm going to try it again.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.620
I couldn't make it to the top.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.620
I want to see the scenery there 
with all our friends next time.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:45.980
Our friends?

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.790
Oh, yeah! Want to come with us to Mt. Fuji?

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.260
The season's over this year, 
so it'll be next year.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.850
What do you think?

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:58.010
I'll go.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.590
Great! Let's go to the top together!

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:03.140
I can't wait.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.140
<b>I want everyone to be happy and healthy 
I want to make it to my first choice high school 
Health first 
Harutaka for the win! 
I want to run faster 
I want to live every day to the fullest</b>

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.150
<b>Akagi Shrine</b>

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:11.900
<b>Good Luck Charm</b>

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:17.680
<b>Hiking Charms</b>

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.720
These charms are cute.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.160
Our trips will all be good from now on.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.070
Yes!

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.100
What's going on?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.440
Are they shooting for TV or something?

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.300
Today we're visiting Akagi Shrine 
in Maebashi, Gunma.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.140
Isn't that...

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.120
Hey, Kokona-cha— Huh?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.210
<i>Gunma-chan!</i>

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.350
<i>Gunma-chan!</i>

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.510
<i>I finally found you!</i>

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.790
Thanks for inviting me today.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:44.520
I had lots of fun.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.140
I'm glad.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.610
Here's a gift.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.240
It's the local konjac we're famous for.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.520
Thanks! I'll be sure to enjoy it.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.220
See you soon.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:54.110
Yeah.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.090
I'll send you the photos later.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.260
Thanks!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.030
I'll contact you, too.

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.310
Huh? Aoi?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.580
Hinata!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:10.750
Kokona-chan!

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:12.250
Aoi-san!

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.520
This is nice.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.120
We're on the same train.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.070
What a coincidence.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:19.650
Listen to this! I got to meet Gunma-chan!

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.290
Huh?

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.530
They were filming something 
at the shrine as we were leaving.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.510
Really? That's great.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.850
Yeah! My dream came true!

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.080
Oh, right...

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.500
I have a gift for you, Kokona-chan.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.620
A gift?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.900
Gunma-chan!

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.740
Thank you!

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.340
I'll treasure it forever.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.910
You're exaggerating.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.010
How was Mt. Akagi?

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.710
It was fun.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.450
It was a hard climb, though.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.140
You might not have made it.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:51.130
What? That's not true!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.420
We saw sunbeams from the mountain peak.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.990
Sunbeams?

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:56.730
Yes.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:59.750
Didn't you see them from where you were?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:04.280
There was light shining through 
the clouds around noon.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.810
It was really pretty.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.810
Here.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:06.810
Oh!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:08.510
You mean this?

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:09.820
That's right!

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.650
We saw them from Ikaho, too.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.540
Honoka-chan said you don't get 
to see them this clearly too often.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.150
Really?

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:19.620
What is it, Hinata?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.710
Oh, er...

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.640
Nothing.

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:34.220
So there's this really long stone 
stairway at Ikaho Hot Springs.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.750
There are 365 steps in all.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:37.710
Wow!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.730
Right?

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:45.220
It's supposed to be to wish for 365 days a year 
of good business for the hot spring town.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.770
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.480
<i>It's not like we need to 
be together all the time.</i>

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.340
<i>As long as we both have fun,</i>

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.820
<i>that's enough.</i>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>
